WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.280
At first glance, I knew we had

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.560
a beautiful sign here in the making.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.235
It's definitely a restorable piece.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:18.464
My name is Howie Cohen,
and I run a sign company

00:00:18.464 --> 00:00:22.297
in Utica, New York,
called Just Neon Sign Co.,

00:00:22.297 --> 00:00:24.663
and I've been doing this since 1993.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:27.450
The techniques are the same.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:30.146
The equipment has gotten a lot better.

00:00:30.146 --> 00:00:34.380
There are more gauges,
there's more analytical data

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.530
that we can obtain when we fill the signs,

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:39.172
but essentially the whole process

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:42.183
is entirely the same since the beginning.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.883
This particular sign is
a Hudson Automobile sign.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.140
Hudson was a very popular
make in automobiles

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.720
back in the '40s and '50s.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.570
They're no longer made,
but these signs still exist

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:00.933
and are highly desirable
amongst the collectors.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.410
Signs of this nature at auction

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:08.107
could bring upwards to $20,000 to $30,000.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:12.720
My only task here is to restore the neon.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.460
The dealer that had this sign

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.850
brought this sign to me in
the condition that it is in,

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.126
and I took it upon myself then

00:01:20.126 --> 00:01:24.090
to restore the sign using
the original materials

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:26.531
that were used back in the 1940s,

00:01:26.531 --> 00:01:29.014
which is neon tubing.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.760
When a sign comes in, the first thing I do

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:36.570
is I make paper patterns of
the neon letters to be made.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.420
Once the tracing paper
is attached to the sign,

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:41.217
a black marker can be used

00:01:41.217 --> 00:01:45.120
to outline the beginning
and the end of each letter.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:48.210
The interesting thing about making neon

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:50.550
is we do everything in reverse.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:54.210
So the pattern I make
here has to be reversed

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.313
before I begin making any neon.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:00.630
The most challenging part
of making a good pattern

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:02.850
is making a good tracing.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.910
You have to make sure your
pattern is not going to move,

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.010
that your paper is not going to move,

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:12.000
and it's got to stay that way
through the entire tracing.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.690
The holes where the glass
housings are located,

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.281
if they're off a little bit,

00:02:17.281 --> 00:02:21.140
your neon unit that you
install might not fit,

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:22.080
and that would mean

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.797
that you have to do the
whole thing over again.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.770
Once I have the pattern
made, I can measure out

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:31.383
how many feet of glass
I'm going to be using.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:33.770
The glass tubing that we use

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:37.470
is specifically made for
the neon-sign industry.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.780
It comes in various diameters.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:43.800
This particular one is 12
millimeter in diameter.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.990
If you use a tube that's too large,

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:48.270
you lose some of the detail.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:51.750
If you use a tube too small in diameter,

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:56.310
it would require lots of
transformers to power it.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:59.193
We use a carbide-tip circle cutter

00:02:59.193 --> 00:03:01.251
and a Dremel tool.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.440
With those two tools,

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:07.683
you can make nice, smooth, accurate cuts.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.860
With my fires on, my glass at hand,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.873
I'm going to be shaping the glass.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.855
It takes many years and years and years

00:03:19.855 --> 00:03:22.446
and miles of glass

00:03:22.446 --> 00:03:26.220
before a glass bender could be comfortable

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.543
with making letters.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:33.450
The type of glass we use
is a relatively soft glass.

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:37.440
The fires we use, either
the long ribbon burner

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.870
to make gentle arcs and curves

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.970
or the sharper cannon fire,

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:45.420
which is used to make what
we call double-back bends.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:47.070
The glass will soften,

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:50.880
and then you really have to
apply a little bit of air

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:53.760
by way of your mouth
into the glass tubing,

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.353
which will then keep it round.

00:03:56.866 --> 00:04:00.240
The hose that's in my mouth
is called the blow hose.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.450
Without the blow hose,
it'd be very difficult

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:06.750
to put the proper amount
of air into the glass

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.550
as it's softening.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:11.340
If you don't do this, it will crimp,

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:15.423
and the gas and the electricity
will not flow properly.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:21.270
The biggest challenge of
the glass-bending process

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:24.780
is not to get burned, not to get cut,

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.000
not to burn and then cut yourself,

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.463
or cut yourself and then burn yourself.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:31.650
Everything is a challenge.

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:35.193
There's so many things that
can go wrong in making neon.

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:40.533
Once the glass is bent, it
goes to the bombarding table.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.670
The machine you're seeing is a manifold.

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:48.461
This meters the gas into the tube

00:04:48.461 --> 00:04:50.352
and evacuates the tube,

00:04:50.352 --> 00:04:54.432
and that's where all
the oxygen, water vapor,

00:04:54.432 --> 00:04:56.343
impurities are pumped out.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:59.850
The glass is also heated.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:02.310
It's heated to a very hot temperature.

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:05.335
Upwards of 300 degrees C.

00:05:05.335 --> 00:05:06.934
Very hot.

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:11.100
Once it's that hot,
almost all the impurities

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:13.740
are pumped out of that tube.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:15.843
Then the gas is filled.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:21.450
Once the gas is applied to
the tube and filled properly,

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:24.093
a high voltage can be passed through that.

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:27.480
The high voltage excites the gas,

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.910
and in this case it's argon.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.100
There's also a little drop of mercury

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:36.660
that's added inside the tube
to make the glass fluoresce.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:39.270
When it lights up the proper color,

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:42.483
then you know you had no
leaks and you had no issues.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:48.770
Every neon sign is composed
of a tube sealed at both ends.

00:05:49.238 --> 00:05:51.630
These ends are called electrodes.

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:54.450
It's a metal-to-glass seal,

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:57.895
which allows the electricity
to go inside the tube.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:00.900
Once the tubing is done,

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:03.153
it's time now to mount it on the sign.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:08.130
The sign is a porcelain sign.
It doesn't need painting.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:10.080
It's actually a glass material

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:12.270
that's put over the top of steel,

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:15.963
is actually the surface that
was put on back in 1940.

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:19.110
There are small tube supports,

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:21.810
and then these little wires
are just twisted tight.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:25.683
That's all it takes to
fasten the neon to the sign.

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:29.400
What I have here is a light socket.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:32.460
In the industry, it's
called the glass housing.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:35.070
This is placed inside the sign.

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:38.580
The metal ring is then
fitted onto the threads

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.260
and tightened down.

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:41.945
When the neon sets in there,

00:06:41.945 --> 00:06:45.093
it just makes physical
contact with that spring.

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:47.473
Inside the sign,

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:51.039
there is a 15,000-volt transformer

00:06:51.039 --> 00:06:54.120
powered to 110 primary.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:57.420
That's a lot of voltage,
but the current is very low.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:07:00.630
It's only approximately 30 milliamps.

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:04.773
It won't kill you, but
you'll know it's there.

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:09.990
I installed the glass
housings, the tube supports,

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:12.780
the wiring on the inside,
and the transformer,

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.823
including the power cord and switch.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.060
There's nothing more that makes me happier

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:19.892
than to take a piece of history

00:07:19.892 --> 00:07:22.141
and bring it back to
the original condition

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:25.266
that it was maybe 70 years ago.

00:07:25.266 --> 00:07:27.840
This is the way the sign
came out of the factory,

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.853
and this is the way it's going to be kept.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:34.020
I'm really happy with the
way this thing turned out.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:37.170
The colors are right.
They're nice and bright.

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:38.850
Everything is uniform.

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:41.520
This sign is going to
be a beautiful addition

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:43.920
to the museum of the car collector.

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:45.819
This is a great example

00:07:45.819 --> 00:07:48.994
of a double-sided porcelain sign

00:07:48.994 --> 00:07:51.630
with the theme of automobiles.

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:54.512
In this case, the famous Hudson.

